MTS patch: uniform game-time dilation (setting timeScale, default 1).

Adds server/mtsGameTime.h and includes it in server.cpp and map.cpp right
after minorGems/system/Time.h. The header routes every Time:: call in
those two files through a virtual clock, E + (real - E) / timeScale, so
aging, food/heat drain, decay and regrowth, cooldowns and walking all
slow down by the same factor. Durations and speeds sent to clients (PU,
PM, FX, HX, MX) are converted back to wall seconds; message-flood batches
stay on the wall clock. timeScale = 1 is stock behaviour. See the header
comment for details and docs/research/time-scale.md for choosing a value.

